  "title": "Lovász Path Removal Conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture There is an integer-valued function $f(k)$ such that if $G$ is any $f(k)$-connected graph and $x$ and $y$ are any two vertices of $G$, then there exists an induced path $P$ with ends $x$ and $y$ such that $G-V(P)$ is $k$-connected.",
